Subject: [PATCH 02732/11362] [outer-loop] Route exp4423 partial-verdict
 FAIL-loop to the .410 planner (known-issues)

.409 PHASE A3 (generic first-contact solver -- the sprint's key live-solver capability)
3-fail-SKIPs every milestone: it emits honest_verdict "partial: ..." for a routed-no-level
run, which the conductor reconciler treats as a non-terminal retry token (only
complete:/success:/passed:/shipped: are accepted) -> FAIL x3 -> SKIP. The run itself is
clean (93.7s, routed g50t, logged a missing_verifier_gap). Documented the atomic 5-point
fix (emission + validator + schema + hard-asserting test) for .410; did NOT edit mid-run
(poison-pre-test-gate risk; bounded skip means the conductor progresses regardless).

